Quicksort is a divide and conquer algorithm that uses a pivot element to partition the list into two sublists. It then recursively sorts the sublists. Quicksort has a time complexity of O(n log n) on average, which makes it much more efficient than bubble sort for large lists. However, it is also more complex to implement and may not be as easy to understand as bubble sort.

